# The pointer moves (ADR-0062, section 5): move=dx,dy is a relative move of
# the pointer, down and right positive, sent every 8 ms tick while a stick in
# mode mouse is pushed; the whole pixels go out and the fractions carry on.
# The left stick at 1000 px/s: 8 px a tick, 50 px in all for the 50 ms push
# (the last 2 px at the tick after the release). Up and right at 45 degrees:
# 5.66 px a tick on each axis, 2.83 while the precision button is held (130 to
# 170 ms), up is negative. The right stick, quadratic and smoothed over 40 ms,
# eases in to 500 px/s and glides on after the release, a pixel at a time. The
# jump at 400 ms is the middle of the virtual desktop (0 to 65535). The pointer
# is not a key, so the exit has nothing to let go of.
move=+8,+0@8
move=+8,+0@16
move=+8,+0@24
move=+8,+0@32
move=+8,+0@40
move=+8,+0@48
move=+2,+0@56
